          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In the general terminology of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framing"} framing
            %em 2-framing
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \leq 2
            is a trivialization of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo −
                        %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \Sigma \oplus \mathbb{R}^{2-d}
          %p
            In
            %a{:href => "#Atiyah1990"} Atiyah 90
            the term “2-framing” is instead used for a trivialization of the double of the tangent bundle of a 3-manifold. So this is a different concept, but it turns out to be closely related to the
            %em 3-framing
            (in the previous sense) of surfaces.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
            3-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  2 T X \coloneqq T X \oplus T X
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} fiberwise direct sum
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            with itself. Via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
            embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SO(3) \to SO(3) \times SO(3) \hookrightarrow SO(6)
          %p
            this naturally induces a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+SO%286%29-bundle"} principal SO(6)-bundle
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+SO%286%29-bundle"} principal SO(6)-bundle
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 T X
              always admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lift+of+structure+group"} lift
              to a
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin(6)
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the sum-rule for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stiefel-Whitney+classes"} Stiefel-Whitney classes
              (see at
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Stiefel-Whitney+class#AxiomaticDefinition"} SW class – Axiomatic definition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    w_2(2 T X) = 2 w_0(T X) \cup w_2(T X) + w_1(T X) w_1(T X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
              is assumed
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_1(T X) = 0
              (since this is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
              to having an
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_2(2 T X) = 0 \in H^2(X,\mathbb{Z}_2)
              and since this in turn is the further
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
              to having a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
          %p Therefore the following definition makes sense
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong 2-framing
              in the sense of (
              %a{:href => "#Atiyah1990"}> Atiyah 90
              ) on a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
              3-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+class"} homotopy class
              of a trivializations of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin-group"} spin-group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
              underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney+sum"} twice
              its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
          %p
            More in detail, we may also remember the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            of 2-framings and the smooth structure on collections of them:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi At
                    %mn 2
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Frame
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} At2\mathbf{Frame}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi At
                            %mn 2
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Frame
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi SO
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi Spin
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 6
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    At2\mathbf{Frame} &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{B}SO(3) &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{B} Spin(6)
                    }
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
          %p
            In terms of this a 2-framing on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi o
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{o} \colon X \to \mathbf{B}SO(3)
            is a lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi o
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat {\mathbf{o}}
            in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi At
                          %mn 2
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Frame
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
