                  \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToBounding4Manifolds Relation to bounding 4-manifolds
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Atiyah1990"}> Atiyah
            ) it is shown how a framing on a compact connected oriented 3-manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is induced by a 4-manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial Z \simeq X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            class of bounding 4-manifolds (
            %a{:href => "#Kerler"}> Kerler
            ).
          %p
            Discussion of 2-framing entirely in terms of bounding 4-manifolds is for instance in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Sawin04"} Sawin 2004
          %h3#RelationToStringStructures Relation to String-structures
          %p
            By (
            %a{:href => "#Atiyah1990"}> Atiyah 2.1
            ) an Atiyah 2-framing of a 3-manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is equivalently a
            %br/
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+c-structures"} structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
            is the first
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+class"} Pontryagin class
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  p_1(X) \colon X \to B SO(3) \stackrel{p_1}{\to} K(\mathbb{Z},4)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This perspective on Atiyah 2-framings is made explicit in (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeNaumann"}> Bunke-Naumann, section 2.3
            ). It is mentioned for instance also in (
            %a{:href => "#Freed08"}> Freed, page 6, slide 5
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+manifold"} framed manifold
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p1-structure"}> p1-structure
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+Chern-Simons+theory"} spin Chern-Simons theory
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion of “2-framing” in the sense of framing of the double of the tangent bundle is due to
          %ul
            %li#Atiyah1990
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              %em On framings of 3-manifolds
              , Topology, Vol. 29, No 1, pp. 1-7 (1990) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/atiyahfr.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            making explicit a structure which slightly implicit in the discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of 3d Chern-Simons theory
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %em Quantum field theory and the Jones Polynomial
              , Comm. Math. Phys. 121 (1989)
          %p reviewed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#Young
              M. B. Young, section 2 of
              %em Chern-Simons theory, knots and moduli spaces of connections
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.sunysb.edu/~myoung/CS.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Atiyah"} Atiyah, page 6
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            see also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                , Robert Gompf,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Computer calculation of Witten’s 3-Manifold invariant
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/freedgompf.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregor+Masbaum"}> Gregor Masbaum
                , section 2 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spin TQFT and the Birman-Craggs Homomorphism
                %a{:href => "http://journals.tubitak.gov.tr/math/issues/mat-95-19-2/pp-189-199.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Freed08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                ,
                %em Remarks on Chern-Simons theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.2507"}> arXiv:0808.2507
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/MSRI_25.pdf"} pdf slides
          %p
            and for discussion in the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            from p. 7 on in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geometric+and+topological+structures+related+to+M-branes"} Geometric and topological structures related to M-branes
                II: Twisted
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi String
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String
                and
                = succeed "-structures" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi String
                          %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} String^c
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.5419"}> arXiv:1007.5419
              ).
          %p
            The relation to
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNaumann
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niko+Naumann"} Niko Naumann
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Secondary Invariants for String Bordism and tmf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0912.4875"} arXiv:0912.4875
            %li
              %p
                C. Blanchet, N. Habegger,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregor+Masbaum"} Gregor Masbaum
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Vogel"} Pierre Vogel
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological quantum field theories derived from the Kauffman bracket
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/bhmv.pdf"} pdf
          %p More discussion in terms of bounding 4-manifolds:
          %ul
            %li#Kerler
              %p
                Thomas Kerler,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Bridged links and tangle presentations of cobordism categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9806114"} arXiv:math/9806114
            %li#Sawin04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+F.+Sawin"}> Stephen F. Sawin
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Three-dimensional 2-framed TQFTS and surgery
                %strong 13
                7 (2004) 947-996 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://digitalcommons.fairfield.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1020&context=mathandcomputerscience-facultypubs"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0218216504003536"} doi:10.1142/S0218216504003536
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+F.+Sawin"}> Stephen F. Sawin
                , page 9 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Invariants of Spin Three-Manifolds From Chern-Simons Theory and Finite-Dimensional Hopf Algebras
                %strong 165
                1 (2002) 35-70 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9910106"}> arXiv:math/9910106
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/aima.2000.1935"} doi:10.1006/aima.2000.1935
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (cf. also at
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+Chern-Simons+theory"} spin Chern-Simons theory
          %p and more discussion for 3-manifolds with boundary:
          %ul
            %li#KerlerLyubashenko01
              Thomas Kerler,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volodymyr+Lyubashenko"} Volodymyr Lyubashenko
              = succeed "," do
                %em Non-semisimple topological quantum field theories for 3-manifolds with corners
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Kuperberg"} Greg Kuperberg
              = succeed "&lbrack;" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/4389/381"} MO:a/4389
